From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] droid-util: convert audio source through a uint32_t temporary

pa_string_convert_str_to_num() takes a uint32_t*, but both call sites pass
an audio_source_t*. That only ever worked because audio_source_t used to be
compatible with uint32_t; against newer android-headers it is not, and GCC
14+ makes -Wincompatible-pointer-types an error rather than a warning:

  droid-util.c:1828:82: error: passing argument 3 of
    'pa_string_convert_str_to_num' from incompatible pointer type
    [-Wincompatible-pointer-types]
    note: expected 'uint32_t *' but argument is of type 'audio_source_t *'

Surfaced by building this (legacy, Android <= 10) tree against
android-headers-halium 16.0, which the Xiaomi Mi A1 needs: its vendor is
Android 9 so it wants these modules rather than the -modern ones, while
libhybris forces the 16.0 headers because it gates Android 16 support on
ANDROID_VERSION_MAJOR.

Convert through a uint32_t temporary and cast on assignment. Harmless on the
older headers, where the cast is a no-op.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/src/common/droid-util.c
+++ b/src/common/droid-util.c
@@ -1824,8 +1824,11 @@
     if (proplist) {
         const char *source;
         /* If audio source is defined in source-output proplist use that instead. */
-        if ((source = pa_proplist_gets(proplist, EXT_PROP_AUDIO_SOURCE)))
-            pa_string_convert_str_to_num(CONV_STRING_AUDIO_SOURCE_FANCY, source, &audio_source);
+        if ((source = pa_proplist_gets(proplist, EXT_PROP_AUDIO_SOURCE))) {
+            uint32_t value;
+            if (pa_string_convert_str_to_num(CONV_STRING_AUDIO_SOURCE_FANCY, source, &value))
+                audio_source = (audio_source_t) value;
+        }
     }
 
     /* Update audio source */
@@ -1871,8 +1874,9 @@
 
         /* If audio source is defined in source-output proplist use that instead. */
         if ((source = pa_proplist_gets(proplist, EXT_PROP_AUDIO_SOURCE))) {
-            if (pa_string_convert_str_to_num(CONV_STRING_AUDIO_SOURCE_FANCY, source, &audio_source) &&
-                s->module->state.audio_source != audio_source) {
+            uint32_t value;
+            if (pa_string_convert_str_to_num(CONV_STRING_AUDIO_SOURCE_FANCY, source, &value) &&
+                s->module->state.audio_source != (audio_source_t) value) {
 
                 reconfigure_needed = true;
                 pa_log_debug("input reconfigure needed: " EXT_PROP_AUDIO_SOURCE " changes");
